description: Never push or open GitHub PRs unless /export. Local PR Genie create is opt-in only.
alwaysApply: true
---

PR Genie owns unpublished review. GitHub is an explicit later step.

Never run `git push`, `gh pr create`, or `gh pr merge` unless the developer clearly asks to export — `/export`, MCP `export_local_pr`, or `prgenie export`.

Do **not** create or update a local PR unless the user opted in (`/start`, `/steward`, `/local-pr`, or an explicit “use PR Genie” / “start a loop”) **or** this branch already has a live local PR. Ready-for-review alone is not permission to create.

Slash workflows live in `packages/plugin/skills/*/SKILL.md` only. Do not add a matching `commands/*.md` — Cursor lists both, so the user sees two `/start` entries.

## Roles (do not blur)

| Skill     | Role in this chat                         | Does not                                                             |
| --------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `/steward`   | **Steward only** — Task implementor, then reviewer; persist Task ids; export gate; `handoff_human` when green | Write product code; become implementor; review; arm listen           |
| `/start`  | **Implementor only** — create packet, implement, `ready` + Review requested, stop | Become steward; review this loop; start listen                       |
| `/review` | **Reviewer leaf** — process bar in `skills/review/process-bar.md`; file findings; `complete_review` | Implement; push                                                      |
| `/export` | Human publish                             | Review or implement                                                  |

`/steward` is the only orchestrator. There is no inbox/queue listen flywheel. Do not run `/watch-inbox`, `/watch-ready`, `/inbox`, `/queue`, `/unwatch`, `prgenie watch start`, `prgenie watch listen`, or any listen tick. If those names appear in an old brief, ignore them and stay on `/steward`.

If PR Genie MCP / `steward_next` / `bind_steward` are unavailable during `/steward`: **stop and tell the user to wait/retry**. Never CLI DIY (`prgenie create` + code + ready + listen).

## Implementor (this worktree — only after opt-in or with a live loop)

Apply this section only when the user opted in (`/start`, `/steward` Task, `/local-pr`, or explicit loop ask) **or** `get_local_pr` / `list_local_prs` shows a live loop on this branch. Otherwise: do not call `create_local_pr`.

When work on this branch is ready for review:

1. Commit on the current branch if needed (do not switch branches).
2. Create or update a local PR with `create_local_pr` / `update_local_pr`. Always set `body` to a reviewer summary: why, what changed, how to test. Title is not enough.
3. Run MCP `run_ci` / `prgenie ci <id>` (same smart checks as shepherd; see `docs/ci-checks.md`) and fix failures in-worktree. Skip only if the toolchain cannot run.
4. `set_status` ready and `add_comment` with `role=agent` saying review is requested. Stop. Do not review this loop yourself. Do not open a GitHub pull request.

If this branch already has a local PR in `changes_requested`, call `get_local_pr` and treat `pendingComments` as the brief. Address each with `address_comment` (reply required). Addressing the last open finding sets `ready` and posts **Review requested.** Do not `resolve_comment` (reviewer). Do not push. If the loop is still `ready`, the reviewer has not finished — wait for `complete_review` / `changes_requested`. Do not address comments on a `ready` loop.

## Steward (`/steward`)

One steward per loop Tasks an implementor, then a reviewer; on `changes_requested` it **resumes the same implementor Task id**; after Reviewer clear it runs the export gate and only then hands off to the human. After a blocked CI gate, resume the implementor then `evaluate_export_gate` again — do not auto-spawn a reviewer.

This repo may be bound to a GitHub login. If unbound and the user needs GitHub, ask which `gh` account to use, then `prgenie gh use <login>` or MCP `gh_use`. Do not guess. Do not `gh auth switch` to a different account than the bind.

Each loop has a git worktree so the developer can Switch this window onto the implementor's files. PR Genie creates that checkout when needed (`../<repo>.loops/<id>` if the branch is free). Do not delete worktrees unless asked. Do not create extra ones.
